Z||000000||AutoXer||11-10-2001||08:04 PM||||Hi guys<P>I am pulling my engine for the first time (88 formula) and I ran into a snag.  Where do I separate the wiring harness?  Does the wiring go with the engine or stay with the car?  If it goes with the engine then how do you get it unplugged at the power distribution box?  If with the car do you need to unplug it from all of the injectors?<P>Thanks in advance<BR>Matt<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/eeege//RedFieroRacing.jpg">  <BR>"He ran out of talent about half way through the corner"||||reg||4
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||11-10-2001||08:25 PM||||You can do it whatever way you feel most comfortable with.  The power distribution box will unbolt from the side wall.  It is a 'grommet' where the harness passes thru the firewall.  Inside there will be two or three plugs to undo and with the 'grommet' undone, all can be passed thru to the engine compartment.  Just follow the bundles of wires.<BR>Gary||||reg||12
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||11-10-2001||08:25 PM||||Hey Matt!<BR>Just take a hacksaw and... NO! NO! NO!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Couldn't resist!<BR>Unplug the ECM and feed the wiring out the firewall...<BR>Else, disconnect each sensor and LABLE as you disconnect them...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000003||AutoXer||11-10-2001||08:30 PM||||Thanks guys!<P>||||reg||1
